[114.612, "o", "I built `~/site/index.html`, the shop's \"What can I build this weekend?\" page, served on port 8080. It suggests three projects from the real inventory: a circular-saw cutting track (an afternoon), a live-edge slab board flattened on the router sled (a day), and a bench joined with dowels (a weekend).\r\n\r\nThe page opens with a warning: the table saw has no blade it can use, because the only 8″ blade in the shop is the wrong size and too thick. The miter saw is listed as gone, so all three projects use the circular saw. Specs marked verify and tools not yet checked are flagged, and the page ends with the \"How this page was made\" table and a footer naming sprite-profiles @ 3938d92 (2026-11-20). `curl` returns the page, and the phone-sized screenshot is at `~/site/screenshot.png`.\r\n"]
